acceptance_criteria: "ADR pm-pbyu's grammar table gains an explicit mapping for init, config, schema, and profile (kept, merged, or verb-moved) with rationale; overlaps are resolved on paper (schema presets vs profile archetypes vs config keys); if any spelling moves, follow-up wiring items are filed under pm-n7rr with alias shims per pm-0z7n; Implement the declared workspace init/config/schema/profile routes through the SDK alias registry with permanent root compatibility and persistent npm/Bun acceptance"
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Consolidated init/config/schema/profile under the existing workspace noun through the SDK alias registry, preserving permanent root aliases and SDK/MCP identities; updated discovery, completion, namespace-aware refusals, contracts, documentation and measured token baselines."
expected_result: "Canonical workspace customization must persist through existing SDK behavior, remain discoverable without mandatory packages, and preserve legacy command compatibility and bounded agent orientation."
actual_result: 130 linked tests passed; full-source coverage reached exact 100/100/100/100; isolated npm/npx and Bun/bunx tarball acceptance passed. The one full-run repository-scan timeout passed unchanged on isolated retry. Canonical orientation remains 1102 tokens. Hosted CI and review remain merge requirements; local CLI latency limits were not relaxed.
